{
  "status": "Source qualified for a local test; Windows D3D12 and user acceptance pending.",
  "base_commit": "4f0faf2",
  "scope": "Supplement existing near grass through the actual camera frustum; no new setting, native field, shadow pass or near-root changes.",
  "changes": [
    "24m bounded quadtree tiles with 0.6m fine root spacing, six opaque triangles per patch and at most 128 resident tiles.",
    "Far view off/on follows the existing camera 100m/260m range. Explicit coarsening retains coverage instead of dropping view corners.",
    "Parent roots are an exact subset of fine roots. Fine-only grass fades before the 96m replacement; newly visible roots grow over 0.25s.",
    "12m frustum prefetch margin and immediate planning for camera turns over three degrees.",
    "Near work keeps priority; at most one far worker, four atomic child uploads and five queued buffers. Existing water, option, scenery and world barriers clear all work."
  ],
